PART 3 -- the pre-registered verdicts V1-V2
  [FAIL] V1 [canonical] DEEP REGIME (r/r_M > 2): pooled per-point rms < 0.13 dex AND radial slope < 0.02 dex/dex -- flat scale-free equilibrium, NEW
         measured: N = 1230 points; pooled per-point rms = 0.1741 dex (threshold 0.13; decomposition: between-galaxy 0.1908, within-galaxy after per-galaxy offset removed 0.0447); per-galaxy radial slope mean -0.1417 dex/dex (threshold 0.02; 93/144 negative)
         reading : registered before the run: the scale-free equilibrium (rho ~ r^-2 has no scale) predicts a tight, flat deep residual. The rms clause and the flatness clause are judged TOGETHER as pre-registered; the decomposition verdicts V4a-V4e establish what the failing structure actually is
  [FAIL] V2 [canonical] INNER regime (r/r_M < 0.5) per-point rms EXCEEDS deep rms by > 1.5x -- the mu_2 transition amplifies baryon-feature noise
         measured: inner rms = 0.2404 dex (N = 794), deep rms = 0.1741 dex (N = 1230), ratio = 1.38 (threshold > 1.5)
         reading : the transition amplifies baryon-feature noise (spiral arms, bulge/disc degeneracy, non-circular motions); a FAIL means the noise architecture is NOT transition-amplified -- a different fingerprint than claimed
  [FAIL] V1 [alt] DEEP REGIME (r/r_M > 2): pooled per-point rms < 0.13 dex AND radial slope < 0.02 dex/dex -- flat scale-free equilibrium, NEW
         measured: N = 1346 points; pooled per-point rms = 0.1768 dex (threshold 0.13; decomposition: between-galaxy 0.1934, within-galaxy after per-galaxy offset removed 0.0479); per-galaxy radial slope mean -0.1329 dex/dex (threshold 0.02; 98/150 negative)
         reading : registered before the run: the scale-free equilibrium (rho ~ r^-2 has no scale) predicts a tight, flat deep residual. The rms clause and the flatness clause are judged TOGETHER as pre-registered; the decomposition verdicts V4a-V4e establish what the failing structure actually is
  [FAIL] V2 [alt] INNER regime (r/r_M < 0.5) per-point rms EXCEEDS deep rms by > 1.5x -- the mu_2 transition amplifies baryon-feature noise
         measured: inner rms = 0.2453 dex (N = 710), deep rms = 0.1768 dex (N = 1346), ratio = 1.39 (threshold > 1.5)
         reading : the transition amplifies baryon-feature noise (spiral arms, bulge/disc degeneracy, non-circular motions); a FAIL means the noise architecture is NOT transition-amplified -- a different fingerprint than claimed

PART 4 -- V3: the environmental EFE test on the repo's real g_ext tables
  [FAIL] V3 [canonical] ENVIRONMENTAL EFE OFFSET: strong-field outer-bin offset > 0.05 dex at the registered 0.5-a0 split; sample-range fallback: d(delta)/d log10 e_N < 0 at p < 0.05 on either g_ext axis (L240 additive-law sign)
         measured: g_ext > 0.5 a0: N = 0 galaxies -- the registered 0.5-a0 split is OUT OF THE SAMPLE'S RANGE (max e_N = 0.0048); offset = n/a (0 strong-field galaxies). Sample-range regressions of the deep-regime mean residual vs log10 e_N: repo 2MRS/2M++ (maxclu): slope -0.0515 +/- 0.0538 dex/dex (p = 0.340, N = 152); Chae+2021 published: slope -0.1071 +/- 0.1079 dex/dex (p = 0.324, N = 93)
         reading : the additive law (L240/G006) predicts strong-field galaxies sag LOW beyond the cap. SPARC is a field sample: its entire e_N range sits an order of magnitude below 0.5 a0, so the registered split cannot fire here -- recorded as the finding that the EFE offset is NOT ESTABLISHED in SPARC, with the directional regressions on two independent g_ext axes as the sample-range test. The architecture's measurable prediction moves to e_N ~ 1 (BIG-SPARC/WALLABY)
  [FAIL] V3 [alt] ENVIRONMENTAL EFE OFFSET: strong-field outer-bin offset > 0.05 dex at the registered 0.5-a0 split; sample-range fallback: d(delta)/d log10 e_N < 0 at p < 0.05 on either g_ext axis (L240 additive-law sign)
         measured: g_ext > 0.5 a0: N = 0 galaxies -- the registered 0.5-a0 split is OUT OF THE SAMPLE'S RANGE (max e_N = 0.0048); offset = n/a (0 strong-field galaxies). Sample-range regressions of the deep-regime mean residual vs log10 e_N: repo 2MRS/2M++ (maxclu): slope -0.0502 +/- 0.0535 dex/dex (p = 0.350, N = 153); Chae+2021 published: slope -0.1137 +/- 0.1070 dex/dex (p = 0.291, N = 94)
         reading : the additive law (L240/G006) predicts strong-field galaxies sag LOW beyond the cap. SPARC is a field sample: its entire e_N range sits an order of magnitude below 0.5 a0, so the registered split cannot fire here -- recorded as the finding that the EFE offset is NOT ESTABLISHED in SPARC, with the directional regressions on two independent g_ext axes as the sample-range test. The architecture's measurable prediction moves to e_N ~ 1 (BIG-SPARC/WALLABY)

PART 5 -- V4: the autocorrelation kill-test and its decomposition
  [FAIL] V4 [canonical] DEEP-REGIME RADIAL COHERENCE: pooled lag-1 autocorrelation < 0.4 -- the kill-test (per-point-noise equilibrium ~ 0; radially coherent errors 0.7+)
         measured: pooled lag-1 AC = +0.838 over 128 galaxies (threshold 0.4); null distribution (within-galaxy circular shifts, 2000 draws): mean +0.225, 95th pct +0.258; p(data >= null) = 0.0000
         reading : registered before the run: the kill-test of the no-halo reading. A FAIL establishes that the deep residual is NOT per-point noise; the decomposition verdicts below establish WHAT the coherent structure is
  [PASS] V4a [canonical] DECOMPOSITION: the coherence is a slow per-galaxy drift, not radial fine structure -- linear-detrended pooled lag-1 AC < 0.4
         measured: raw +0.838 -> after removing each galaxy's own best-fit line in log(r/r_M): +0.018 (threshold 0.4); after a 3-pt running-median detrend: -0.222
         reading : removing ONE straight line per galaxy collapses the autocorrelation to ~0: the deep-regime residual is one quasi-static per-galaxy offset/drift plus WHITE per-point noise. There are no coherent rings or bumps to fit -- the halo-shape error mode (an NFW concentration wiggle) leaves no trace in the residual's radial structure
  [PASS] V4c [canonical] the drift's SIGN is population-coherent: galaxies with sagging deep residuals exceed 50/50 (binomial p < 0.01)
         measured: 83/128 galaxies have a negative drift slope (0.648); binomial p vs 0.5 = 0.001
         reading : random per-galaxy systematics (distance, inclination, M/L) would split evenly; a one-sign population drift is the signature of a MONOTONIC external/background effect shared by the sample
  [PASS] V4d [canonical] the population mean drift differs from zero: t-test p < 0.01, registered sign sag LOW
         measured: mean drift slope = -0.1310 dex/dex, t = -3.80, p = 0.00023 (N = 128 galaxies)
         reading : the deep-regime residual is FLAT point-to-point but SAGS systematically toward the outermost self-similar radii -- a real, small, one-sign radial structure that any deep-regime account must absorb
  [FAIL] V4e [canonical] ATTRIBUTION of the drift to the external field at SPARC amplitudes: d(drift)/d log10 e_N < 0 at p < 0.05 on either axis
         measured: repo axis: +0.0067 +/- 0.1176 dex/dex per dex (p = 0.955, N = 144); Chae published: +0.2450 +/- 0.2039 dex/dex per dex (p = 0.233, N = 90)
         reading : at SPARC's field strengths (median e_N ~ 0.003) the additive law's own shift is ~0.001-0.01 dex -- an order of magnitude below the measured ~0.1-dex drift -- so no attribution at this amplitude is expected; the regression quantifies that honestly. The attribution test that CAN decide it lives at e_N ~ 1 (BIG-SPARC/WALLABY)
  [FAIL] V4 [alt] DEEP-REGIME RADIAL COHERENCE: pooled lag-1 autocorrelation < 0.4 -- the kill-test (per-point-noise equilibrium ~ 0; radially coherent errors 0.7+)
         measured: pooled lag-1 AC = +0.848 over 138 galaxies (threshold 0.4); null distribution (within-galaxy circular shifts, 2000 draws): mean +0.237, 95th pct +0.263; p(data >= null) = 0.0000
         reading : registered before the run: the kill-test of the no-halo reading. A FAIL establishes that the deep residual is NOT per-point noise; the decomposition verdicts below establish WHAT the coherent structure is
  [PASS] V4a [alt] DECOMPOSITION: the coherence is a slow per-galaxy drift, not radial fine structure -- linear-detrended pooled lag-1 AC < 0.4
         measured: raw +0.848 -> after removing each galaxy's own best-fit line in log(r/r_M): +0.069 (threshold 0.4); after a 3-pt running-median detrend: -0.172
         reading : removing ONE straight line per galaxy collapses the autocorrelation to ~0: the deep-regime residual is one quasi-static per-galaxy offset/drift plus WHITE per-point noise. There are no coherent rings or bumps to fit -- the halo-shape error mode (an NFW concentration wiggle) leaves no trace in the residual's radial structure
  [PASS] V4c [alt] the drift's SIGN is population-coherent: galaxies with sagging deep residuals exceed 50/50 (binomial p < 0.01)
         measured: 91/138 galaxies have a negative drift slope (0.659); binomial p vs 0.5 = 0.00023
         reading : random per-galaxy systematics (distance, inclination, M/L) would split evenly; a one-sign population drift is the signature of a MONOTONIC external/background effect shared by the sample
  [PASS] V4d [alt] the population mean drift differs from zero: t-test p < 0.01, registered sign sag LOW
         measured: mean drift slope = -0.1380 dex/dex, t = -4.34, p = 2.7e-05 (N = 138 galaxies)
         reading : the deep-regime residual is FLAT point-to-point but SAGS systematically toward the outermost self-similar radii -- a real, small, one-sign radial structure that any deep-regime account must absorb
